8. Queue ≠ necessarily an in-memory data structure
A beginner might imagine:
Queue<Message> queue = new LinkedList<>();
A distributed message broker needs to solve:
Memory
+
Persistence
+
Concurrency
+
Network communication
+
Failure recovery
+
Replication
+
Ordering
+
Acknowledgement tracking
So the broker often has components resembling:
Producer
   |
   v
Network Layer
   |
   v
Broker
   |
   +---- Queue / Log
   |
   +---- Persistence
   |
   +---- Replication
   |
   +---- Consumer state
   |
   v
Network Layer
   |
   v
Consumer
