For a message M1, think of its lifecycle:
CREATED
   |
   v
SENT
   |
   v
ACCEPTED
   |
   v
PERSISTED
   |
   v
DELIVERED
   |
   v
PROCESSING
   |
   v
PROCESSED
   |
   v
ACKNOWLEDGED
But failures can move it backward:
DELIVERED
    |
    v
CONSUMER CRASH
    |
    v
REDRIVE
    |
    v
DELIVERED AGAIN
This state-machine perspective is much more useful than memorizing Kafka/RabbitMQ APIs.
