When designing any asynchronous system, ask these questions in order:
1. Why asynchronous?
        ↓
2. What is the message?
        ↓
3. Who produces it?
        ↓
4. Where is it stored?
        ↓
5. Who consumes it?
        ↓
6. When is it considered successfully processed?
        ↓
7. What happens if consumer crashes?
        ↓
8. What happens if producer retries?
        ↓
9. What ordering is required?
        ↓
10. What durability is required?
        ↓
11. What happens when consumers are slower than producers?
        ↓
