If you partition by restaurantId instead of orderId, you may get good restaurant locality, but what happens when the same restaurant has thousands of orders concurrently?
If you partition by orderId, you get excellent distribution and per-order ordering.
So the key question is:
What is the actual unit of ordering?
That question should become almost automatic in your system-design thinking.
