31. But partitions aren't simply "worker threads"
This is an important architectural distinction.
A partition represents:
ordered log
not merely:
worker slot
Increasing partitions affects:
ordering boundaries
producer parallelism
consumer parallelism
replication
storage
recovery
metadata
So don't choose partition count solely from:
"How many consumers do I want?"
You need to consider the entire system.
